3.10.text:
Article 34

Forms of PPT services for women and children who are victims of acts of violence, include:
a. medical services, in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of women and children who are victims of acts of violence carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medical services for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;
c. psychosocial services;
d. legal services to assist women and children who are victims of acts of violence in undergoing legal processes; and e. economic independence services in the form of skills training and providing economic access so that women and children who are victims of acts of violence can be independent.

Article 18

1. The Regional Government implements efforts to prevent acts of violence against women and children through:a. implementation of policies for prevention of acts of violence against women and children in accordance with policies established by the Government;
b. establishment of policies, programs and activities for prevention of acts of violence against women and children;
c. formation of PPT;
d. awareness to families, parents and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling;
e. increasing the quantity and quality of education, both formal and non-formal and informal;
f. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
g. opening employment opportunities for women;
h. seeking participation and concern of the community to implement prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
i. development and provision of a complete and easily accessible information system;
j. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; andk. opening complaint posts for protection and prevention of acts of violence against women and children.
2. Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by Regional Apparatus that administer government affairs in the fields of:a. women's empowerment and child protection;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. social;
f. mental and spiritual; andg. peace and order.
3. Prevention by regional apparatus as referred to in paragraph (2) is coordinated by the Agency. (4) Prevention of violence by regional apparatus as referred to in paragraph (2) is implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on RAD.

Article 28

1. Services for assistance and recovery of women and children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 25 are provided to women and children who are domiciled in the Region and who experience violence within the Region.
2. Forms of assistance and recovery services as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out in the form of:a. women's empowerment;
b. child rehabilitation;
c. complaint, consultation and counseling services; and d. assistance services.
3. Provisions regarding the form and procedures for assistance and recovery services for women and children who are victims of acts of violence shall be further regulated in a Mayor Regulation.

Article 16

1. Implementation of protection for women from acts of violence is carried out through activities:a. prevention of acts of violence;
b. assistance and recovery services for women who become victims of acts of violence;
c. reunification; andd. empowerment of women who become victims of acts of violence.
2. Implementation of protection of children from acts of violence is carried out through activities:a. prevention of acts of violence;
b. handling services for children who become victims of acts of violence;
c. reunification; andd. rehabilitation of children who become victims of acts of violence.
3. Implementation of protection as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is carried out by the Regional Government through the Agency.

Article 2

The scope of this regional regulation includes: a. acts of violence;
b. implementation of protection;
c. implementation of prevention of acts of violence against women and children;
d. implementation of services, assistance and recovery for women and children who become victims of acts of violence;
e. institutions;
f. reunification;
g. empowerment and rehabilitation;
h. guidance and supervision; andi. financing.

Article 4

The purpose and objectives of implementing protection of women and children from acts of violence include:
a. prevention of acts of violence against women and children;
b. handling services, assistance and recovery for women and children who become victims of acts of violence;
c. reunification; andd. empowerment of women and rehabilitation of children who become victims of acts of violence.

Article 37

The provision of services and assistance to women and children who are victims of acts of violence is carried out with the principles of:
a. fast, safe and empathetic;
b. guarantee of confidentiality;
c. easily accessible; and
d. free of charge.

Article 25

1. Every woman and child who becomes a victim of acts of violence has the right to receive:a. protection;
b. information;
c. optimal services;
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. confidential handling;
f. psychological and legal assistance; and g. guarantee of rights related to status as a family member and community member.
2. The Regional Government guarantees the fulfillment of the rights of women and children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1).

Article 12

1. The Regional Government implements protection efforts for women and children from acts of violence through:a. implementing protection policies for women and children from acts of violence applied by the Government;
b. establishing policies, programs and activities for protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. formation of PPT;
d. ensuring the implementation of service facilities for women and children who become victims of acts of violence;
e. seeking effectiveness and efficiency for the recovery process of women and children who become victims of acts of violence; andf. seeking the creation of cooperation and coordination in the recovery efforts for women and children who become victims of acts of violence.
2. In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, the Regional Government establishes action programs and activities for protection of women and children from acts of violence in 1 (one) RAD as a basis for regional apparatus in implementing protection for women and children who become victims of acts of violence.
3. RAD as referred to in paragraph (2) constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.
4. RAD as referred to in paragraph (2) is further regulated by Mayor Regulation.

Article 4

The purpose and objectives of providing protection for women and children from acts of violence are to:
a. prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children from acts of violence; and
d. facilitate and mediate domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

